    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0248" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg152"/>

                <head>No. 94.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hurlbut to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogota</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 16, 1872</date>,
                        (Received March 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 74.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of my final note to Señor
                    Zapata of the 9th instant. To this I have received a reply stating that
                    instructions have <pb facs="0249" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/> been forwarded to
                    Senor Perez for the conduct of the matter at Washington. I hardly see what more
                    is left to be argued. There is a demand and a refusal, and one party or the
                    other must yield. I venture to express the wish that the final decision of this
                    matter may be communicated through me to the Colombian government, as it was
                    commenced by me.</p>
                <p>Yours, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. A. HURLBUT.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d94-a1.xml" xpointer="d94-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
